<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy | Zone Two Health and Performance"
  description="How Zone Two Health and Performance collects, uses, stores and discloses your personal and health information."
  eyebrow="Privacy Policy"
  heading="Privacy and Collection of Personal Information"
>
  <p>
    At Zone Two Health &amp; Performance, we are committed to protecting your privacy and
    maintaining the confidentiality of your personal and health information.
  </p>

  <p>
    We collect information that is necessary to provide safe, effective and coordinated
    healthcare. This may include your personal details, medical history, medications, imaging
    reports, referral information, lifestyle factors and other health information relevant to
    your care.
  </p>

  <h2>How your information is used</h2>
  <p>Your information is used to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>assess your health and provide treatment</li>
    <li>develop appropriate management plans</li>
    <li>communicate with other healthcare providers involved in your care</li>
    <li>
      prepare reports, referral letters, medical certificates and other clinical documentation
    </li>
    <li>
      process health fund, Medicare, DVA, WorkCover, CTP or other insurer claims where
      applicable
    </li>
    <li>comply with legal and professional obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How your information is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Your information is stored securely using electronic practice management systems and
    appropriate administrative, technical and physical safeguards. Access is limited to
    authorised members of our clinical and administrative team who require the information to
    perform their duties.
  </p>

  <h2>When information may be disclosed</h2>
  <p>
    Your personal information will not be disclosed to another person or organisation without
    your consent unless:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>disclosure is required or authorised by law;</li>
    <li>
      it is necessary to prevent a serious threat to your life, health or safety, or that of
      another person;
    </li>
    <li>
      it is required for Medicare, insurers, WorkCover, CTP, DVA or other lawful purposes
      directly related to your care.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Accessing and correcting your records</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access to your health records or request corrections if any information is
    inaccurate or incomplete, subject to applicable legislation.
  </p>

  <h2>Your consent</h2>
  <p>
    By signing this form, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy
    Statement and consent to Zone Two Health &amp; Performance collecting, using, storing and
    disclosing your personal information for the purposes outlined above in accordance with the
    Privacy Act 1988 (Cth), the Australian Privacy Principles and the Health Records and
    Information Privacy Act 2002 (NSW).
  </p>

  <h2>Online booking and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses Cliniko, a secure Australian practice management system, to provide online
    appointment booking. When you use the booking pages, the Cliniko booking system sets functional
    cookies that are necessary for the booking process to work. These include a session identifier
    and a browser identifier. No marketing, advertising or analytics cookies are set by the
    booking system.
  </p>
  <p>
    Booking data you enter (such as your name, contact details and selected service) is processed
    by Cliniko and stored on servers located in Australia. For further information, refer to
    <a href="https://www.cliniko.com/policies/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Cliniko's Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    This website does not use cookies for any other purpose. No analytics, advertising or
    tracking cookies are set by this website.
  </p>

  <nav class="legal__next" aria-label="More on privacy">
    <a href="/privacy/data-security">Electronic health records and data security</a>
    <p>More detail on the practice management system that stores your records.</p>
  </nav>
</Legal>
